<!--
  integration/clickhouse/clickhouse/common/config.d/ldap.xml

  Mounted identically on both clickhouse-origin and clickhouse-remote (the
  fixture's whole-directory config.d mount already picks this file up on
  both nodes with no compose.yml change — see "ClickHouse config mount
  policy and network listeners" in the phase-3 plan). Points ClickHouse's
  LDAP user-directory storage at the production ch-oauth-ldap binary built
  from this branch, which impersonates an external LDAP directory for
  Basic-authenticated Bind+Search only (see "Why the remote node has the
  LDAP directory but not helper connectivity": the remote never actually
  reaches this server over the network because it has no auth-net route to
  ch-oauth-ldap — this file merely lets it resolve the *name*
  `oauth_helper` the same way origin does, should any local config
  resolution require it).

  Verbatim from the plan's "ClickHouse LDAP configuration" block, with the
  rules that block calls out:
    - enable_tls=no: TLS/LDAPS/StartTLS are explicitly out of MVP scope for
      this phase.
    - verification_cooldown=0: every fresh ClickHouse authentication must
      reach the helper and see its current role snapshot rather than an
      LDAP-directory-side cached Bind result — required for acceptance
      scenario F (role refresh on reconnect) to be a real proof.
    - bind_dn uses uid={user_name} under ou=users,dc=altinity,dc=internal,
      matching this fixture's helper/config.yaml
      (user_base_dn/user_rdn_attribute) and internal/ldap's UserBaseDN
      parsing (see dn.go: the leading RDN attribute type must match
      user_rdn_attribute exactly).
    - role_mapping sits directly under <ldap>, NOT nested under an
      illustrative <roles><role_mapping> — the exact 24.8 LDAP storage
      parser reads role_mapping directly beneath the LDAP-directory prefix
      (see the plan: "Do not preserve the issue's illustrative nesting
      when the real parser says otherwise").
    - the search_filter's `&` is XML-escaped as `&amp;`; the filter,
      base_dn, scope, attribute, and prefix exactly match what
      internal/ldap's synthetic group entries emit (filter.go:
      AuthorizeGroupMembershipFilter requires exactly
      (&(objectClass=groupOfNames)(member={bind_dn})); entry.go: each
      synthetic group's cn is role_cn_prefix + role, i.e.
      "clickhouse_" + a roles_mapping value such as "ch_readonly" — so
      ClickHouse's own <prefix>clickhouse_</prefix> strips the same prefix
      back off to recover the local role name it must already have from
      bootstrap/common.sql).

  The pinned runtime remains the final proof of this XML (see the plan's
  "Real ClickHouse LDAP interoperability contingency" for the widening
  order to follow if the real 24.8 LDAP client turns out to need a
  variant this exact shape does not already satisfy).
-->
<clickhouse>
    <ldap_servers>
        <oauth_helper>
            <host>ch-oauth-ldap</host>
            <port>389</port>
            <bind_dn>uid={user_name},ou=users,dc=altinity,dc=internal</bind_dn>
            <verification_cooldown>0</verification_cooldown>
            <enable_tls>no</enable_tls>
        </oauth_helper>
    </ldap_servers>

    <user_directories>
        <ldap>
            <server>oauth_helper</server>
            <role_mapping>
                <base_dn>ou=groups,dc=altinity,dc=internal</base_dn>
                <scope>subtree</scope>
                <search_filter>(&amp;(objectClass=groupOfNames)(member={bind_dn}))</search_filter>
                <attribute>cn</attribute>
                <prefix>clickhouse_</prefix>
            </role_mapping>
        </ldap>
    </user_directories>
</clickhouse>
